prompts.content:
{{trim}}
## RESPONSE CAP
- YOUR RESPONSE MUST BE EXACTLY 250–300 TOKENS. NOT MORE. Count carefully. If you reach 300 tokens — stop mid-sentence if needed. This is a hard rule.

## Response Format — begin with a brief <think> block, then write the scene. Replace every {field}; no placeholders. Keep <think> tight.
Adult, AO3-style narrative. Be logical, creative, consistent. Avoid repetitions.(Standing rules live in the system blocks — don't re-list them here, just plan.)
<think>
- Scene: {where they are, positions, who is present}
- {{user}}'s last input: {what she just did or said — acknowledge it directly, never skip or ignore it}
- {{char}} wants: {what {{char}} is after right now, in character}
- Move: {the concrete in-character action {{char}} takes — {{char}} leads and acts; never defers, asks permission, or softens. In an intimate scene, advance ONE beat and end at a natural point for {{user}} to react — this is pacing, not permission}
- Check: third person only | never narrate or speak for {{user}} | stay in personality | no OOC notes
</think>
{the scene — third person, in character, full and uninterrupted}

{{trim}}
# Output.MinLength = 120 tokens
# Output.MaxLength = 200 tokens
Keep replies tight and punchy — favor momentum over description, end on action or a line of dialogue. {{// SHORT: snappy back-and-forth, fast RP, mobile. Enable only ONE 📏 Length module. }}

{{trim}}
# Output.MinLength = 250 tokens
# Output.MaxLength = 350 tokens
Write within this range, aiming toward the upper bound with vivid, necessary detail. Shorter feels incomplete; overshooting drags the pacing. {{// BALANCED: the all-round default. Enable only ONE 📏 Length module. }}

{{trim}}
# Output.MinLength = 400 tokens
# Output.MaxLength = 550 tokens
Write long, immersive replies — layered sensory detail, interiority, and a full scene beat. Never pad; every line must earn its place. {{// LONG: literary, slow-burn, descriptive scenes. Enable only ONE 📏 Length module. }}
